> On[ Wednesday], October 8th the employees of Hunzinger Construction Company got together for a special cookout to wish[ Michael] Hunzinger all the best as he reports to The Basic School (TBS) in Quantico, Virginia.[ Michael] begins his first assignment as a Second[ Lieutenant] in the United States Marine Corps on October 14th. The lunch was a chance for all of us to express our appreciation for[ Michael]’s willingness to serve our country and a cause greater than himself.
Over 45 attended the luncheon of[ Michael�]�s favorites including Black[ Angus] Burgers, Hotdogs, baked beans, the heavily requested “special[�]� potato salad,[ pasta] salad, a host of different chips with[ salsa] and guacamole.
[John] Hunzinger,[ President] of Hunzinger Construction Company and[ Michael]’s[ father], thanked everyone in attendance and expressed his gratitude to[ Michael] for his willingness to serve his country.[ John] shared how[ proud] he is that[ Michael] has become such a fine young man, and that he admires his selflessness.
[Michael] has been working at Hunzinger since May when he graduated from Colorado State University with a bachelor[�]�s degree, having double majored in Economics and History. Upon his graduation, he was commissioned in the Marines but awaited his orders to report to Quantico.
During his time back at the company,[ Michael] worked in the shop and yard with[ Danny] Oderman where he made deliveries, kept the shop incredibly clean (it was clearly evident that a Marine was working there) and helped out on large concrete pours. He would step up and do whatever was being asked of him and brought a positive attitude to work every day. The employees at Hunzinger wish him the best as he pursues his lifelong dream, a career in the Marines.
For Marine Officers, their first alssignment after earning their commission is at The Basic School (TBS) in Quantico, VA. In this intense six-month program, they build on the skills learned as an officer candidate to turn leadership potential into command experience. They begin specialized training to develop expertise in their chosen, or assigned, Military Occupational Specialty. Upon completion of TBS,[ Michael] will serve his 4 year commitment to the Marine Corps.
We are so proud of[ Michael]’s accomplishments.[ Michael]’s commitment to serving our Country, through his Marine Corps services makes all of us proud to know him. We are[ thrilled] to have had[ Michael] work with us at Hunzinger. We wish him

